export const placeholders = "<p class=\"pn\">Rust-colored words in brackets are filled in for each reader. The value after the colon is only an example. Every slot comes from the quiz she already took or from her birth date. Nothing new is asked.</p>\n\n<h3>All slots at a glance</h3>\n<table>\n<tr><th>Slot</th><th>Where</th><th>Value</th><th>If missing</th></tr>\n<tr><td><code>NAME</code></td><td>Sales page, chat, pop-ups 1 and 5</td><td>First name from the quiz, first letter capitalized.</td><td>Drop the name and the comma after it.</td></tr>\n<tr><td><code>BIRTH_DATE</code></td><td>Sales page, chat, pop-up 2</td><td>Written like <em>March 4, 1979</em>. In the chart label it’s all caps.</td><td>Never missing (the quiz asks for it).</td></tr>\n<tr><td><code>SIGN</code> · <code>ELEMENT</code></td><td>Sales page, chat, pop-up 1</td><td>Sun sign and its element. The sign badge at the top also shows that sign’s symbol (♈︎ ♉︎ ♊︎ ♋︎ ♌︎ ♍︎ ♎︎ ♏︎ ♐︎ ♑︎ ♒︎ ♓︎).</td><td>Never missing.</td></tr>\n<tr><td><code>VENUS_SIGN</code></td><td>Sales page (Venus tile), pop-up 1</td><td>The sign Venus was in on her birth date. Same tool that works out her sun sign. No birth time needed.</td><td>Never missing.</td></tr>\n<tr><td><code>AREA</code></td><td>Sales page, chat</td><td>From “What matters most to you right now?”: Love → <em>love</em>, Work → <em>work</em>, Finance → <em>money</em>, General → <em>a bit of everything</em>.</td><td>Use <em>a bit of everything</em>.</td></tr>\n<tr><td><code>TURN_STATE</code></td><td>Sales page: headline, facts line, closing, P.S. Chat: step 6.</td><td>Days until <strong>November 13</strong> (US Eastern): <em>in N days</em>. On November 12: <em>tomorrow</em>.</td><td>See the date rule below.</td></tr>\n<tr><td><code>MERCURY_LINE</code></td><td>Sales page</td><td>Before Oct 24: <em>On October 24, Mercury goes retrograde too.</em> From Oct 24: <em>Since October 24, Mercury has been retrograde too.</em></td><td>Never missing.</td></tr>\n<tr><td><code>MERCURY_LINE_CHAT</code></td><td>Chat</td><td>Before Oct 24: <em>Mercury goes retrograde too on October 24.</em> From Oct 24: <em>Mercury’s been retrograde too since October 24.</em></td><td>Never missing.</td></tr>\n<tr><td><code>ASTROLOGER</code></td><td>Chat header</td><td>Real astrologer’s name, plus a real photo where “NK” is. Nora Keating is a stand-in.</td><td>Needed before launch.</td></tr>\n<tr><td><code>MONTH_AHEAD</code></td><td>Chat</td><td>Next month’s name, e.g. <em>November</em>.</td><td>Write <em>booked for weeks</em> instead of <em>booked into November</em>.</td></tr>\n<tr><td><code>ASTROVEO_LEGAL_NAME</code> · <code>ASTROVEO_ADDRESS</code> · <code>SUPPORT_EMAIL</code></td><td>Footer of both pages</td><td>Your legal details.</td><td>Needed before launch.</td></tr>\n</table>\n\n<h3>Date rule: when the sales page stops being true</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Both pages say Venus “is retrograde” and count down to November 13. That’s true up to <strong>November 12</strong>.</li>\n<li><strong>On November 13, stop or swap both pages.</strong> The sales page and the chat both say the retrogrades are still on, so neither is true after November 12.</li>\n<li>Every date on both pages is the same for every reader. Only the slots above change.</li>\n</ul>\n\n<h3>Paragraph slots, by quiz answer</h3>\n<table>\n<tr><th>Slot</th><th>Answer</th><th>Text</th></tr>\n<tr><td rowspan=\"4\"><code>ELEMENT_LINE</code></td><td>Fire</td><td>You’re a fire sign. You move first and think about it on the way, and when you’re in, you’re all in. That’s a gift. It’s also why a year that won’t move hits you harder than most.</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Earth</td><td>You’re an earth sign. You build things slowly and you build them to last, and you’re the one everybody leans on. That’s a gift. It’s also why you hate waiting on things you can’t control.</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Air</td><td>You’re an air sign. Your mind is always 3 steps ahead, and you can talk yourself into or out of anything. That’s a gift. It’s also why you second-guess the moves that matter most.</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Water</td><td>As shown on the page.</td></tr>\n<tr><td rowspan=\"12\"><code>VENUS_LINE</code><br><small>Starts with “Your Venus is in [VENUS_SIGN].”</small></td><td>Aries</td><td>You go after what you want and you don’t play games about it. Waiting on someone else to make up their mind is the one thing you can’t stand.</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Taurus</td><td>You love slow and you love for keeps. Once you’re in, you’re loyal to a fault, and you stay longer than you should when it’s not working.</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Gemini</td><td>You need someone who can keep up with you. When the talking stops, you check out, even if everything else is fine.</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Cancer</td><td>You take care of the people you love before they even ask. You also keep quiet score, and it hurts when nobody does the same for you.</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Leo</td><td>You love big and you want it to show. You don’t need much, but you do need to feel chosen, out loud.</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Virgo</td><td>You show love by doing things: fixing, planning, remembering. You notice every little thing people do, and it stings when they don’t notice yours.</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Libra</td><td>You’re the one who keeps the peace. You’ll bend a long way to keep things nice, and sometimes you only notice how far after it’s too late.</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Scorpio</td><td>You don’t do halfway. You let very few people all the way in, and when someone breaks that trust, you don’t forget it.</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Sagittarius</td><td>You need room to breathe, even from people you love. The minute it starts to feel like a cage, part of you is already halfway out the door.</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Capricorn</td><td>You take love seriously and you don’t hand it out to just anyone. People think you’re cool at first. The ones who stay find out you’re the most loyal person they know.</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Aquarius</td><td>You need space even from people you love, and someone has called that cold. You love on your own terms, and the right people get that.</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Pisces</td><td>You love with your whole heart and you see the best in people, sometimes more than they’ve earned. You’ve given second chances you knew you shouldn’t.</td></tr>\n<tr><td rowspan=\"2\"><code>DEPTH_LINE</code></td><td>Yes / Sometimes</td><td>As shown on the page.</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Not really</td><td>You told us people mostly get you. That’s rarer than you’d think, and it means that when you finally ask for something, people listen.</td></tr>\n<tr><td rowspan=\"2\"><code>GIVING_LINE</code></td><td>Yes / Sometimes</td><td>As shown on the page.</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Not really</td><td>You’re careful about where your time and energy go. This fall, that matters more than usual.</td></tr>\n<tr><td rowspan=\"4\"><code>AREA_LINE</code></td><td>Love</td><td>As shown on the page.</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Work</td><td>You picked work. For you, work has run stop-and-start this year. You’ve put in the effort and watched it go unnoticed, or go to somebody else, and you’re tired of waiting to be picked.</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Finance</td><td>You picked money. For you, money has come in and gone out this year without ever quite adding up. Every time you got a little ahead, something came along and took it back.</td></tr>\n<tr><td>General</td><td>You picked a bit of everything, which usually means more than one thing needs to move. For you, 2026 has been a year of almost: close on a few fronts, finished on none.</td></tr>\n<tr><td rowspan=\"2\"><code>PATTERN_LINE</code></td><td>Yes / Sometimes</td><td>As shown on the page.</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Not really</td><td>Most people hit the same wall more than once, even when they don’t call it a pattern.</td></tr>\n<tr><td rowspan=\"4\"><code>SEASON_LINE</code><br><small>Under the 6-week sky chart</small></td><td>Love</td><td>As shown on the page.</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Work</td><td>For work, retrograde is a time to finish and fix what you’ve started. Hold off on big new moves until it ends on November 13.</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Finance</td><td>For money, retrograde is a time to review and tidy up. Hold off on big buys until it ends on November 13.</td></tr>\n<tr><td>General</td><td>Retrograde is a time to finish, fix and reconnect. Hold off on big new starts until it ends on November 13.</td></tr>\n<tr><td rowspan=\"2\"><code>AREA_BOLD</code><br><small>Under “You said [AREA]”</small></td><td>Love / Work / Finance</td><td>If it’s [AREA], you need to know your luckiest day to go after it. If it’s something else, you need to know that even more, or you’ll spend the luckiest week of your year pushing on the wrong door.</td></tr>\n<tr><td>General</td><td>Whatever it is, you need to know your luckiest day to go after it, or you’ll spend the luckiest week of your year pushing on the wrong door.</td></tr>\n</table>\n\n<h3>Pop-up 4, one version per report item</h3>\n<p class=\"pn\">Same layout and button as pop-up 4 on the Pop-ups board. Only the heading and text change.</p>\n<table>\n<tr><th>Item</th><th>Heading</th><th>Text</th></tr>\n<tr><td>01</td><td>Which part of your life this retrograde is in</td><td>Venus retrograde happens in 1 part of your chart, and that’s where you feel it most. Your Transformation Window Report names it.</td></tr>\n<tr><td>02</td><td colspan=\"2\">As shown on the Pop-ups board.</td></tr>\n<tr><td>03</td><td>Your lucky days and your days to hold off</td><td>Some days before November 13 are still lucky for you, and some are better for laying low. Your Transformation Window Report marks each one on 1 calendar.</td></tr>\n<tr><td>04</td><td>Your luckiest day</td><td>1 day between November 13 and 19 is your luckiest. Your Transformation Window Report names it, with the best hours that day.</td></tr>\n</table>\n\n<h3>For the build</h3>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Her birth chart</strong> is drawn for each reader from her birth date (noon, since there’s no birth time). Venus and Mercury are added in orange where they are today. The chart on the board is a sample for March 4, 1979.</li>\n<li><strong>Anything with a box around it</strong> on the sales page is either a real button or has an orange number. <strong>Orange numbers</strong> are tap targets. Each one opens the pop-up with that number, sliding up from the bottom.</li>\n<li><strong>“See my full reading”</strong> (under the chart and after her horoscope) opens pop-up 5. Every “Get my Transformation Window Report” button goes straight to checkout.</li>\n<li><strong>The facts line</strong> under the sky chart is plain text on purpose, so it doesn’t look tappable.</li>\n<li><strong>The chat</strong> follows the “How the chat sells” board step by step.</li>\n<li>Log every pop-up open and every chat question tap, so the next heatmap shows which ones lead to sales.</li>\n</ul>\n\n<h3>Need from you</h3>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Report contents.</strong> Both pages promise 4 things: which part of her life this retrograde is in; who’s coming back and whether to give them a second chance; her lucky days and days to hold off; her luckiest day with the best hours. Confirm or tell me what to cut.</li>\n<li><strong>Report delivery.</strong> The pages don’t say how or when the report arrives. Tell me and I’ll add 1 line under the buy button.</li>\n<li><strong>Astrologer</strong> name and photo for the chat.</li>\n<li><strong>Testimonials and star ratings</strong> are samples. Swap in real ones or remove them.</li>\n</ul>\n";
